MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replay existed because the inputs a decision saw were not recorded, so they
had to be rebuilt after the fact — and every rebuild has a hole the prod runs
found one at a time: research snapshots expire after 120 days, a sale since
the decision loses the price and makes the row unreplayable, the probe budget
can only be inferred by sensitivity analysis, and yesterday's decision was
being replayed under today's settings (the design's "largest unquantified
risk", FARM2-VERIFICATION §7.3). This records the inputs instead.

A `decisionInputs` sub-document on AutoFarmTask, version 1: the research the
gate was given (demandScore, sellers, scannedAt — or null, with an unscanned
document kept distinct from no document), the sales exactly as salesOf()
returned them (count, revenue, avgPrice), an af fingerprint of every setting
the sellability stage, probe gate and tier target read, the probe gate's two
outputs, and the market floor as a recorded value (it also depends on
marketplace keys, so it is not re-derived).

One shape, three writers, one reader. utils/decisionInputs.js is the only
definition; autoFarmer.processCampaign, the lane's decide step and replay all
import it and none describes it themselves.

Legacy: a single `let recordedInputs` in processCampaign, populated the moment
alloc is known and spread into record()'s $set — so EVERY record() call on
EVERY path writes it, including reuse_existing and skip_host_offline (the two
that never wrote internalSales), with no per-call-site edits. skip_reuse_only
keeps the farm-time snapshot from the same tick. A re-decided RETRYABLE row
gets a fresh snapshot each tick. This is the first commit in the series to
touch the body of processCampaign: one require plus ~12 lines. Apply onto
prod's copy with git am -3.

Lane: decideCampaign builds the same object and carries it on every verdict;
execute.js persists it from upsertTask and executeReuse, so a lane-created
row is replayable exactly like a legacy one.

Replay: reconstructInputs checks the snapshot FIRST. A recognised version is
taken whole — exact fidelity, no gaps, no SaleSignal query, no snapshot
lookup, no probe sensitivity check — and the recorded af fingerprint
overrides today's for the fields it covers, so recorded rows replay under the
settings then in force. Every row reports inputsBasis (recorded |
reconstructed) and inputsVersion; the summary and CLI show the split;
afAssumed is now labelled as applying to reconstructed rows only.

Absence is never a passing value. A snapshot that exists but is not recognised
(a later version, a malformed write) is reconstructed and carries
decision_inputs_version_unknown — not trusted, not silently ignored. A row
with no snapshot is reconstructed exactly as before, with no gap.

Deliberately NOT recorded: pool depth, capacity, host state, archive coverage —
the downstream gates' inputs. Replay's scope is unchanged. Nothing for rows
written before this ships.

AutoFarmTask declares the sub-schema (strict mode would otherwise drop it on
$set — the model's own comments warn of this three times). af is Mixed so a
setting can be added under the same version. ~200 bytes per row.

processCampaign is exported (additive) so a test can drive the real record()
on the three branches that need no host: the sellability skip, the host gate
and the dry-run reuse.

19 new tests. Suite 691/692 vs the de4facd baseline of 672/673; the single
failure (dropSetsListLight) is pre-existing and unchanged.
